                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>Insights:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>* 93% of respondents reported that their final construction cost exceeded their initial estimate.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>* The average reported overrun was approximately 10.4%.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>* 10.8% of respondents with known final costs experienced an overrun of more than 20%.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>*</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'> 41% of respondents reported unexpected/unplanned expenses or unexpected repairs/issues.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>* </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>The average confidence in the initial budget estimate was 3.87/5, suggesting that homeowners had moderate-to-high confidence despite widespread overruns.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>* Homeowners were relatively confident in their initial estimates (3.87/5), yet 93% reported going over budget.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
